		<pubDate>Thu, 21 Jun 2012 22:53:53 +0000</pubDate>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=919#comment-12020</guid>
		<description><![CDATA[I first knew Maharaji in Philadelphia in the early 1970&#039;s.  He was my son&#039;s godfather. I have always valued his unerring devotion to Hazrat Inayat Khan and his commitment to living &quot;outside the system&quot;. He was an idealist and I find inspiration in the way he carried through on his beliefs, even to the end.  My children and I are deeply saddened by his death, he was a powerful presence.]]></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>I first knew Maharaji in Philadelphia in the early 1970&#8217;s.  He was my son&#8217;s godfather. I have always valued his unerring devotion to Hazrat Inayat Khan and his commitment to living &#8220;outside the system&#8221;. He was an idealist and I find inspiration in the way he carried through on his beliefs, even to the end.  My children and I are deeply saddened by his death, he was a powerful presence.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
